{"id":"G2079","lemma":"ἐσχάτως","transliteration":"eschatōs","sayIt":"eschatōs","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"extremely","meaning":"ἐσχάτως\nadv.,\nextremely, utterly; ἐ. ἔχειν (= Lat. in extremis esse), only in late writers (cf. ἐν ἐσχάτοις εἶναι, FlJ, Ant., ix, 8, 6), to be at the point of death: Mrk.5:28.†\n(AS)","glosses":["near death"],"count":1,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mrk-5","v":23,"renderings":{"bsb":"near death","kjv":"lieth"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Mark 5:23","note":"and begged him much, saying, “My little daughter is at the point of death. Please come and lay your hands on her, that she may be made healthy, and live.”","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G1722","lemma":"ἐν","transliteration":"en","gloss":"in/on/among"},{"id":"G20790","lemma":"μωκός","transliteration":"mōkos","gloss":"mocker"},{"id":"G20791","lemma":"μωλωπικός","transliteration":"mōlōpikos","gloss":"suitable for weals"},{"id":"G20792","lemma":"μώμημα","transliteration":"mōmēma","gloss":"blame"},{"id":"G20793","lemma":"μῶν","transliteration":"mōn","gloss":"are you?"},{"id":"G20795","lemma":"μωροπόνηρος","transliteration":"mōroponēros","gloss":"stupidly wicked"},{"id":"G20796","lemma":"ναῦλος","transliteration":"naulos","gloss":"rent"},{"id":"G20797","lemma":"νάφθα","transliteration":"naphtha","gloss":"naft"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}